      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which the quadratic expression \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we need to assume that the quadratic expression can be factored as \\( (x + p)(x + q) \\). Expanding this product, we get:\n\\[ x^2 + (p+q)x + pq. \\]\nBy comparing coefficients with the given quadratic expression \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\), we see that:\n\\[ pq = 2008 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad b = p + q. \\]\nWe need to find all pairs of integers \\((p, q)\\) such that \\( pq = 2008 \\) and then determine the corresponding values of \\( b = p + q \\).\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of 2008. The prime factorization of 2008 is:\n\\[ 2008 = 2^3 \\times 251. \\]\nThe factor pairs of 2008 are:\n\\[ (1, 2008), (-1, -2008), (2, 1004), (-2, -1004), (4, 502), (-4, -502), (8, 251), (-8, -251). \\]\nFor each pair \\((p, q)\\), the value of \\( b = p + q \\) is:\n\\[ 1 + 2008 = 2009, \\]\n\\[ -1 - 2008 = -2009, \\]\n\\[ 2 + 1004 = 1006, \\]\n\\[ -2 - 1004 = -1006, \\]\n\\[ 4 + 502 = 506, \\]\n\\[ -4 - 502 = -506, \\]\n\\[ 8 + 251 = 259, \\]\n\\[ -8 - 251 = -259. \\]\nThe smallest positive value of \\( b \\) from the above calculations is 259. Therefore, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients is:\n\\[ \\boxed{259}. \\]",
