      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which the quadratic expression \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) can be factored into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we need to consider the form of the factors. If the quadratic expression can be factored as \\( (x + p)(x + q) \\), then the constant term must be the product of the constants in the binomials, i.e., \\( 2008 = pq \\). Also, the sum of the constants in the binomials must be the coefficient of the linear term, i.e., \\( b = p + q \\).\n\nWe need to find the smallest positive \\( b \\) such that there exist positive integers \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) satisfying \\( p + q = b \\) and \\( pq = 2008 \\).\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of 2008. The prime factorization of 2008 is:\n\\[ 2008 = 2^3 \\times 251 \\]\n\nWe list all the factor pairs \\((p, q)\\) where \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) are positive integers:\n\\[\n(1, 2008), (2, 1004), (4, 502), (8, 251)\n\\]\n\nAmong these pairs, the pair \\((8, 251)\\) gives the smallest sum:\n\\[ p = 8, \\quad q = 251 \\]\n\\[ b = p + q = 8 + 251 = 259 \\]\n\nWe need to verify that \\( 2008 = 8 \\times 251 \\) and \\( 259 = 8 + 251 \\), confirming that these are valid factor pairs. Therefore, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{259}\n\\]",
